Cerberus evolved from MetaRouter v3 (the MetaRouter v4 lineage).
MetaRouter v3 used free-claude-code as an architectural reference:
(an open-source Claude Code proxy project; architectural reference only)
The donor notice states that its initial implementation copied no source files.
Cerberus copyright and MIT license are in LICENSE.

Fusion mode delegates deliberation to OpenRouter's Fusion Router, an external
API integration. Cerberus redistributes no OpenRouter source or assets.
Releases before 0.01 bundled a modified managed Fusion (MIT) worker; that component
and its provenance material are no longer part of this repository.
